Updates: the family updater instead of the embedded Sparkle.

The old Sparkle framework is not bundled (maintainer decision 2026-11-07). This
removes the imports, the appcast defaults iTerm2 wrote for Sparkle, and Sparkle's
version comparator, replaced by iTermFamilyVersionIsNewer
(product/iTermFamilyVersion.m), which orders versions the same way for the four
incompatible-software checks. The two Sparkle checkboxes in General preferences are
hidden. checkForUpdates: launches the family updater, ITERM_UPDATER_BUNDLE_ID (from
shipyard's product registry), with --user; if it is not installed, or cannot be opened,
an alert says which and names ITERM_RELEASES_URL.

Upstream's restart handling stays: Sparkle's will-restart notification sets
sparkleRestarting, so a quit for an update leaves restorable sessions' jobs running
for the relaunch. The family updater runs in its own process, so the notification
now comes from its post-update helper (product/restart-for-update.m) on the
distributed center. Since any process in the session can post there, the flag
counts for 60 s only (MavericksiTerm2UpdateRestartSeconds overrides it) and a
declined quit clears it. Once a quit begins within that window, its decision
holds however long the quit prompt stays open. The app acknowledges the
notification, and the helper quits it only after that acknowledgement, since
the helper's quit request may otherwise arrive first. A declined quit tells the
helper, which then stops waiting.

